{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1000", "sample_idx": 17, "model_name": "abacusai/dracarys-llama-3.1-70b-instruct", "content": "Raymond III Count of Tripoli was the Count of Tripoli from 1152 to 1187. He was the son of Raymond II Count of Tripoli and Hodierna of Jerusalem. Raymond III succeeded his father as count in 1152. In 1158 he married Eschiva of Bures daughter of William of Bures Prince of Galilee. They had no children.\n\n*Early Life and Reign*\nRaymond III was born in 1130s in Tripoli. He was the eldest son of Raymond II and Hodierna. Raymond II was killed in 1152 by the Hashshashin. Raymond III succeeded his father as count and his mother acted as regent until he came of age.\n\nIn 1157 Raymond III was captured by the Hashshashin while traveling from Tripoli to Tortosa. He was released after a ransom was paid. In 1164 he participated in the Battle of Harim where the Crusader forces were defeated by the Zengid forces led by Nur ad-Din Zangi.\n\n*The Marriage and Alliances*\nIn 1158 Raymond III married Eschiva of Bures daughter of William of Bures Prince of Galilee. The marriage was arranged by King Baldwin III of Jerusalem to strengthen the alliance between the Kingdom of Jerusalem and the County of Tripoli. Raymond III and Eschiva had no children. In 1174 Raymond III became regent of the Kingdom of Jerusalem for the underage King Baldwin IV.\n\n*The Battle of Hattin and Later Life*\nIn 1187 Raymond III participated in the Battle of Hattin where the Crusader forces were defeated by the Ayyubid forces led by Saladin. Raymond III was one of the few Crusader leaders who escaped the battle. He fled to Tyre where he died in 1187. He was succeeded as count by his godson Raymond IV Count of Tripoli son of Bohemond III of Antioch.", "logprobs": [{"token": "Ray", "logprob": -0.004134069196879864}, {"token": "mond", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": " III", "logprob": -6.318112355074845e-06}, {"token": " Count", "logprob": -0.35264554619789124}, {"token": " of", "logprob